%SIXMD 1
# @?RM - REMOVE FILES

## @?OPERANDS

### @?FILE ...
ONE OR MORE FILES OR DIRECTORIES TO REMOVE.

### @?-R
REMOVE DIRECTORIES RECURSIVELY, INCLUDING THEIR CONTENTS.

### @?-F
IGNORE MISSING PATHS.

### @?--
END OPTION PROCESSING.

## DESCRIPTION

WITHOUT -R, RM UNLINKS NAMED NON-DIRECTORY FILES. WITH -R, RM
TRAVERSES DIRECTORIES AND REMOVES THEIR CONTENTS BEFORE REMOVING
THE DIRECTORY ITSELF. SYMBOLIC LINKS ARE NOT FOLLOWED.

RM -R REFUSES THE ROOT DIRECTORY, DOT, AND DOT-DOT AS OPERANDS.
DIRECTORY TRAVERSAL IS BOUNDED TO 16 LEVELS. FAILURES ARE REPORTED.
-F SUPPRESSES LOOKUP AND ORDINARY UNLINK ERRORS, INCLUDING MISSING
PATHS; IT DOES NOT SUPPRESS ERRORS AFTER RECURSIVE DELETION BEGINS.

USAGE IS 'RM [-R] [-F] [--] FILE ...'.

## @?EXIT STATUS

### @?0 - SUCCESS
### @?1 - OPERATION FAILED OR CONDITION FALSE
### @?2 - INVALID USAGE WHEN APPLICABLE
